# Legacy UI — do not test

The legacy wizard at `/legacy` (`templates/index.html`, `src/web/static/documents_ui.js`, related legacy fixtures) is **deprecated**.

## Do

- Test and fix the **React SPA** (CampaignFlow) and its APIs (`/api/v1/*`, campaign/document flows as wired in the new UI).
- Treat document generation and mailing paths that still only exist behind legacy as **known debt** — note in reports, do not expand manual/E2E coverage of `/legacy`.
- Prefer removing or shrinking legacy surface over adding features to it.

## Do not

- Manual QA walkthroughs of `/legacy`
- New Playwright/e2e/visual coverage aimed at the legacy wizard
- New features or UX polish in legacy templates/JS
- Telling the user to “check in legacy” as the primary path

When legacy must be mentioned (e.g. explaining an architectural gap), say it is scheduled for removal and point to the React path instead.
